  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1215 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nTonight into Friday night\n\nA 1025 mb surface high, currently over the western Dakotas and \neastern Montana, will gradually build east across the Upper \nMississippi River Valley. Skies will gradually clear tonight and \nthen this high will provide mostly clear skies and light winds into \nFriday night. \n\nLow temperatures tonight and Friday night will range from the mid-\n30s to mid-40s. There may be some patchy to areas of frost in \ncentral and north-central Wisconsin. High temperatures on Friday \nwill be in the lower 60s.\n\nSaturday and Saturday night\n\nA Canadian cold front will approach the area from the Northern \nPlains on Saturday and then move southeast through the area on \nSaturday night. There should be enough moisture convergence for \na few showers to form along the front north of Interstate 90.\n\nHigh temperatures will be in the lower and mid-60s. Low \ntemperatures will range from the lower 40s to lower 50s.\n\nSunday through Tuesday\n\nHigh pressure will provide dry weather. High temperatures will be in \nthe lower and mid-60s on Sunday and Monday, and in the mid- to upper \n60s on Tuesday. Low temperatures on Sunday and Monday nights will \nrange from the mid-30s to mid-40s. There may be some patchy to areas \nof frost in central and north-central Wisconsin.\n\nTuesday night into Wednesday\n\nAnother Canadian cold front will move east through the area. There \nremains much uncertainty on whether there will be any rain with this \nfront. Low temperatures will range from the mid-40s to mid-50s. High \ntemperatures will range from the upper 60s to mid-70s.",
